WEBVTT

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:29.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.820
If what you say is true,

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.350
this could possibly kill Wendelin.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:38.780
However...

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.260
Head Auditor Ruckner deeply 
regrets providing you

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.750
with mistaken information before,
 so this time...

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.820
So how much do you intend to take?

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.320
No money will be necessary.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:51.920
Huh?!

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.420
We simply ask that once you become the lord,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.430
you show us favor during negotiations for 
the interests in the undeveloped lands.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.520
I see.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.990
So he wants my cooperation as a 
fellow man in a difficult position.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.310
Here comes that asshole Kurt.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.250
Well, he should have heard that Well was 
entering the undeveloped lands by himself.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.050
Does this mean that information 
actually reached him?

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.960
We did go around telling everyone we could.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.930
Now the plan to make your brother 
blow up is entering its final stages.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:45.250
But the man that approached 
him already left, right?

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.090
I was convinced that he was going 
to bring an assassin with him.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.900
But he's coming by himself.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.360
Which probably means he's found 
some chance of beating you.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.360
Brother Kurt, what are you doing here?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.190
Cut the act.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.320
They're here, right?

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.010
<i>Grk!</i>

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.980
Come out, you damned retainers!

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.140
I know you're there!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.900
Wendelin... you certainly are amazing.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.530
Huh?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.400
You've defeated a dragon,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.610
you've been showered with 
praise as a great magician,

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.820
and now you're attempting to 
become the next lord of this land.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.280
But still...

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.480
You're the eighth son, not the eldest!

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.970
Don't move!

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.380
If you move, I'll blow this Dragon's Flute!

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.840
What?! How did you...

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.300
I suppose a veteran magician 
like you would know of it.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.260
This is my first time seeing 
the real thing, though.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.110
Brantag?

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.250
The Dragon's Flute is a magic item 
uncovered from ancient ruins.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.910
You can summon dragons by blowing on it.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.940
But we've faced dragons before.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.190
Not en masse.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.440
Every single one in the Great 
Rieg Mountains will rush down here.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.170
Even the boy's magic power 
won't last if that happens.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.920
I guess even the heroic Dragon Slayer
 can't prevail against sheer numbers.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.360
What the hell are you laughing about?!

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.040
If you do that, you won't be safe, either!

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.930
Come now, are you an idiot?

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.510
Do you think I'd ever use a magic item that 
would cause its user to be attacked, too?

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.470
But if that many dragons come, 
the people here will suffer!

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.810
Those bastards betrayed me!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.390
They should reap what they sow!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.690
B-B-But your family would die, too!

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.900
I can just start a new family!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.610
What are you saying?

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.760
Listen to me. I'm going to steal your assets,

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.250
make the development happen,

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:07.280
and become an even greater hero than 
you in these undeveloped lands!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.080
Once I've done that, women will 
flock to me on their own.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.130
So long as I have another son 
after that, all will be as it was.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.750
My stupid brother...

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.710
Don't move! I'll blow it!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.130
That's it! That's what I wanted to see!

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:30.090
The thing I've always hated the most was 
that condescending attitude of yours!

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.600
I've always wanted to ruin 
that look on your face!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.100
Ah, finally!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.180
Wendelin, just remember this.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:50.490
The deaths of our people, of Amalie, 
and of all your precious comrades,

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.450
are all your fault!

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.550
Looks like this flute, at least, is on my side.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.870
It's my victory in the end!

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.800
Die, Wendelin!

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.300
What are you doing?!

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:28.950
No!

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.160
I have a really bad feeling about this.

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.870
That's malice.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.960
Huh? I thought it was going to call dragons?

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.290
I thought something was off.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.730
The Dragon's Flute is a legendary magic item.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:48.260
It's not something so easily obtained.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.300
Then Brother Kurt was deceived?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.220
Most likely, that's the Flute of Malice.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.110
Once you blow it,

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:59.560
it draws in malice from the surroundings 
so you can defeat your enemy,

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.190
eventually turning you into an 
undead, and with that power...

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.400
Wait a second! It turns its user into an undead?

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:10.580
Those who come in contact with 
malice will perish. Which means...

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.570
No way...

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.200
<i>Why?!</i>

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.520
<i>Why don't things ever go as planned?</i>

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:22.500
<i>Why won't anybody listen to me, the eldest son?!</i>

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.400
<i>They all play me for a damn fool!</i>

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.010
<i>They mock me, the eldest son!</i>

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.560
<i>They'll pay for that! They'll pay!</i>

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.430
<i>So help me, they will pay for doing that to me!</i>

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.780
Boy, use your holy magic!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.160
What's the matter?! He's already dead!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.370
Brother...

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.210
I'll purify him!

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:13.760
There's too much malice.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.050
At this rate, everyone will...

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.010
I won't let...

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.210
anyone else...

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.340
Keep it up!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.820
Expand the purification magic like 
we did in the Enchanted Forest.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.280
But...

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:35.240
My, that's impressive, Head Auditor Ruckner.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:39.590
To think you would recognize 
Sir Roderich as insurance against

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.450
the failure of Baron Baumeister's assassination.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:47.390
Regardless of what he may want, 
he's still my son, after all.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.350
If you use that connection, 
you can eat into the new land interests.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.890
Still, I want that country 
bumpkin to work hard for me

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:01.110
so I can put one over on my brother,

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.810
but with his abilities...

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:06.250
He's nothing more than a disposable pawn?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.710
There are so many incompetent men 
who ride on their status as eldest son.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.830
Are you... Kurt?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.490
I see. So the one who gave 
that flute to Brother Kurt was...

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:43.520
As a result, he and twelve 
other nobles of the robe,

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.580
along with their relatives, 
lost their lives in that incident.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.460
What a villain.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.040
By the way, the malice 
believed to have been Kurt

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.420
has already been purified by the priests.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.520
They're still investigating the cause,

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:00.470
but it's believed that a fragment 
of the malice you purified

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.390
was guided here by his hatred.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.850
I also have one other thing to report.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.030
Rumors have been spreading 
around the capital that

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:15.080
the one behind this incident was Sir Kurt.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:20.930
I know you had planned for Lady Amalie 
and her children to live here, but...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.780
I see. They'd be the family of a criminal.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.770
So even if they were to move here,

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:30.300
they would find it even more 
uncomfortable than their home.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.500
I think it would be a struggle 
for them to live in the capital.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.880
So where did they end up?

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.120
They're living in hiding with the second son.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.920
But some of the people 
still view them with hostility

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.810
because they're Brother Kurt's family,

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.170
so they can hardly even go outside.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.970
Hey, want a drink? It's mead.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:01.390
People keep calling me the heroic 
Dragon Slayer and putting me on a pedestal,

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.720
but this is the real truth.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.740
I couldn't save a single person.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:09.800
What could you have done?

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.660
It's the Flute of Malice.
No one could've seen that coming.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.730
Speaking of which, we tried to 
determine how he obtained that flute,

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:19.920
but none of our searches 
are turning up solid leads.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:25.090
Maybe that was all a part 
of the palace's plot, too.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.640
I'm so sick of all that nonsense.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.950
Everyone's sneaking around behind my back,

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.130
and I have no idea who's plotting what,

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.970
or what they're after...

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:35.600
It just never ends.

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:38.860
Yet despite all that, they keep all 
the crucial details hidden in shadow

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.320
and never take any responsibility.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.390
What is wrong with these nobles?

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.240
You know, boy, I've had 
this thought for a while,

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:53.950
but every now and then,
you talk like you're not yourself.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:57.710
Huh? I don't think I do that...

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.880
You do.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.630
Just now, you said all 
those things about nobles,

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.930
but take a good look in the mirror.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:08.260
You're a noble yourself, remember?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:22.790
This is good!

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:23.540
Which one?

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:24.200
This one.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.720
Let me have some!

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.720
Yours looks good, Iina!

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.980
Wanna try some?

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:27.820
Don't mind if do.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:28.670
Hey, let's trade!

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:29.540
Sure.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:41.300
Hey, does it feel like I'm barely here?

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.380
Barely here?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.040
Uh, maybe I'm not saying it right,

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:49.720
but does it seem like I'm 
out of touch with reality?

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.350
Or maybe there's a better way to put it...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.700
This might be something different,

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.480
but sometimes I do feel anxious.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:01.310
It feels like you're far away, 
even though you're close by.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:05.780
I guess it's because I haven't 
accepted this world.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:11.180
I thought I had prepared 
myself to face it, though.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:27.440
Elise, I think I'm going to try to
become a proper noble here.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:34.450
You always did have a habit of saying

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.650
you'd do your best, and do it smartly.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.770
You'll be fine.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.160
I'm sure you can become one.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:49.240
Wendelin von Benno Baumeister...

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:55.200
You truly served well in quelling the 
incident in the Baumeister Knightdom.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.740
Therefore, I shall grant you 
all the undeveloped land

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.170
confiscated from the Baumeister Knightdom.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:04.130
I humbly accept.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:05.840
However...

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.590
It would be unkind of me to reward your 
achievements with land that comes tied

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.830
with the obligation of laboring to develop it.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:13.640
So, Sir Baumeister,

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.600
what would you wish to have for a reward?

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:22.020
This was proposed to me by 
Lord Commissioner Ruckner.

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:30.040
We did saddle the baron with a great deal 
of trouble for his family's mistake.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.700
It's the least we could do to make up for it.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:38.120
To be honest, there was something 
I wished to ask for, too.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.830
Oh? Let me hear it.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.940
I have heard that twelve nobles of the robe

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:46.540
perished in the incident 
caused by the Flute of Malice,

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:52.800
and that many are currently calling upon 
the capital, seeking to claim the open titles.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:58.520
This is true. Every day, there's a 
rabble of self-proclaimed relatives.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:04.980
There are even some among the late 
nobles who lost all of their relatives.

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:08.880
So for the sake of developing 
the vast, undeveloped lands,

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:13.700
I would like to be given the right 
to grant two of those open titles.

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:20.040
The right to grant titles 
belongs solely to the king.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:23.250
This is insolent, Sir Baumeister!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:26.500
To think you would treat His Majesty's 
consideration with such disdain!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:33.490
Granting such a large swath of land to 
a mere baron is already unthinkable!

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:37.970
Asking for the right to grant nobility on 
top of that couldn't be more audacious!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.680
Rescind that request, now.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.360
There's no need to rescind it!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.400
Your Majesty, please forgive me, but I must say...

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:50.890
Granting Sir Baumeister only a 
portion of those undeveloped lands

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:54.000
and granting the rest to someone more 
experienced in managing a domain

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.560
would be of greater benefit to our kingdom.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:59.460
But Sir Baumeister's magic 
is necessary to develop it.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:01.330
How about Baron Mark?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.980
He may not be able to use magic,

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.060
but he's the greatest 
developer in the kingdom.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.330
Hold on.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:11.500
That man is one of your 
close relations, Sir Edgar.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.540
You always focus too much on such details!

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.350
Gentlemen, you stand before our king.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.040
Besides, if memory serves,

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.640
there have been past cases where the right 
to grant titles was bestowed on another.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.620
Those were all cases with 
pressing reasons to do so.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.610
So the idea should at least be considered.

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:36.000
You are Sir Baumeister's lord.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:40.500
You only say such things because you 
hope to expand your own faction!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.620
I do not!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.580
I am simply thinking of our kingdom.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.790
We are also thinking of the kingdom.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.570
Is that truly so?

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.750
What insolence is this?!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.420
Be silent!

00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:00.600
Sir Baumeister, rescind your request.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.210
Magician, please listen—

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.790
Can you not see what you've done?!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:09.520
Your reckless actions have upset 
the order of the royal palace!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:13.480
You lack a noble's decorum, Sir Baumeister!

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:19.110
Your Majesty, if I may.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:22.100
As Lord Marshall Edgar proposed,

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.610
could we not grant Sir Baumeister a portion 
of the undeveloped land he's due to receive,

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.670
and place the remainder under my care?

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:32.130
I will develop it myself.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:36.090
True, a magician as great as you could...

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.710
Everyone!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.280
Magician Armstrong,

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.970
you are needed here in the capital.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.240
But great magic power is needed 
to develop those lands!

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.980
Which is why we shall have 
Sir Baumeister develop them.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:59.330
Development of those undeveloped lands 
is our kingdom's greatest priority.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:02.800
We need him to put his fullest effort into it.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.660
So if this will secure that...

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.870
Then you'll bestow the right to grant titles?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.250
<i>Gulp!</i>

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.930
Sir Baumeister, raise your head.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:27.600
As you wish, I shall bestow upon 
you the right to grant two titles.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.810
I thank you for your generosity.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.770
You're starting to look like a real noble now.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:41.950
In addition, I, Helmut XXXVII,
 King of Helmut Kingdom,

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:45.940
hereby grant thee, 
Wendelin von Benno Baumeister,

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:50.910
the fifth rank and title of Count 
to develop those lands.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.880
He jumped straight past viscount to count?!

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.930
My sword shall be wielded for Your Majesty,

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:02.000
for our kingdom,

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.840
and for our people.

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:17.080
That man has grown quite clever.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:18.730
Clever?

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:22.450
Everyone performed well except you.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.410
You should practice your acting.

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:29.870
That so?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.940
I think I'll refrain.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:38.250
Once those children come of age,

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.060
I plan to grant them the titles I hold.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:45.720
If they don't need them, 
they're welcome to turn them down.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.010
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:52.640
Sir Wendelin...

00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:00.110
My husband's death was one he chose himself.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:05.070
I'm sure my boys will understand that one day.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:15.020
Thank you, Well.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.210
Entry Forbidden

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.210
Count Baumeister

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:22.670
Entry Forbidden

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:22.670
Count Baumeister

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:22.670
All right, everyone! Get to work!

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:25.300
Yeah!

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:32.010
Your magic is so useful, Well.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:34.060
You flattened everything in an instant.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:40.000
I'll be heading back now, Roderich.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.450
One moment, my lord.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.200
Can you take care of that area next?

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:48.240
Uh, what's going up over here?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:49.340
A church.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.640
The one sponsored by Cardinal Hohenheim.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.290
And the others?

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:57.010
Over there is for Lord Commissioner Ruckner,

00:21:57.010 --> 00:21:59.620
beside it is for Lord Marshall Edgar,

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:03.760
behind those are the facilities 
for Duke Bleichröder...

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.490
Wow, they're getting in 
deep for those interests.

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:09.720
I am indebted to them for securing 
me the right to grant titles...

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:15.760
Though, here, there won't 
be any of that butting in.

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:16.390
Count Baumeister's Personal Miso & Soy Sauce Workshop

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:19.980
Wendelin, I've finished preparing the tea.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.530
Oh, I'm not finished yet.

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:23.820
Well!

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:27.280
Did you forget today's one of our training days?

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:36.200
We made a deal the other day that you'd 
train four days a week in return for my help.

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:39.890
Well, I went into the Enchanted Forest
 and brought this back!

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:43.190
Banana, banana, banana, banana!

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:44.350
Everything in there is huge.

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:48.300
Ba-ba-banana! Bananana! Banana, banana!

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:49.360
Hey, Well, my spear broke and I'd 
like to get it fixed in the capital.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:51.300
Chocolate-covered banana! 
Chocolate, chocolate-covered banana!

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:51.300
Could you teleport me there?

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:53.110
Chocolate-covered banana!

00:22:51.590 --> 00:22:55.260
Hey, shouldn't you prepare the land first?

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:58.980
Hold on, hold on! Don't leave 
me alone with this magician!

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:01.940
Well, make chocolate-covered bananas!

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:08.110
W-W-Wait... just a choco-pickin' minute!

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:08.610
Hey, help me out!

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:10.260
No, I—

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:09.950
Don't leave me hanging!

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:10.260
Hey, hurry up!

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:11.260
Hey!

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:12.620
What am I supposed to do here?!

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:13.630
Prepare the—

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:23.580
Pork ribs fried in miso, 
along with white radish sprouts...

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.550
Time to eat up.

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.650
Let's eat!

00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:31.490
Man, this is so good!

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:33.650
You're right, these are great together.

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:34.560
This is good! So good, so good!

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:36.120
So good!

